!Sample_submission_date = Aug 10 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Mar 18 2021
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = B16 melanoma - in vitro
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = antibody: H3K27ac
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: control
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = CRISPR knock-out (KO) was performed via delivery of CAS9 and sgRNA to B16 cells.  When indicated, cells were selected using standard agents (blasticidin, puromycin, hygromycin). No additional treatments were administered.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = All cell lines were tested for mycoplasma and cultured in RPMI (VWR) or DMEM media (Gibco) supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (FBS) and antibiotics.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = 250,000 cells per sample were fragmented with micrococcal nuclease (MNase) and subjected to T7 adapter ligation and pooling prior to immunoprecipitation with anti-H3K27ac (Active Motif, 39133) antibody and magnetic protein G dynabeads.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Sequencing libraries were constructed via in vitro transcription of adapter ligated DNA followed by reverse transcription/cDNA synthesis and a final library PCR to enrich adapter-modified DNA fragments.
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: MINT_ChIP-seq
!Sample_data_processing = ChIP-seq reads were first trimmed by Trim Galore (v0.4.5) to remove adapter sequences. The trimmed reads were aligned to mm9 by Bowtie (v2.2.2) with the parameters –N 1 –L 25 -X 2000 --no-mixed --no-discordant. All unmapped reads and PCR duplicates were removed. Non-uniquely mapped reads were assigned to the position with the best matched score. For downstream analyses, we normalized read counts by computing the numbers of reads per kilobase of bin per million of reads (RPKM).
!Sample_data_processing = genome build: mm9
